Terra-Shore-Writes: Lares (Tasked Spirit). Read-only diagnosis. Repo: /home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine (span ed193feee) and the b1-lift worktree /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt (head d6c5b494c). Write nothing. Mark claims MEASURED (file:line, log line) or INFER.
packages/lararium-web/tests/e2e/shore-writes.e2e.test.ts reads red in CI for the third time tonight across three lanes (b1-lift twice: runs 42197282289 attempt 1 and 42234220343; b1-seal: 42205053266), each time two cases ("served wiki saves a draft tiddler without worker errors", "the vessel page reports its instruments …") with `page.waitForFunction: Timeout 20000ms exceeded` at waitForLivePage, phases reaching vessel-ready, no faults; it passed on one rerun and 5/5 locally. Excerpt: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/controller/terra-shore-writes/fail-excerpt.log; logs: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/ci-42234220343.log, /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/ci-42197282289.log, /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-seal/ci-42205053266.log. House law: a recurrence reads as a new fault; a race gets pinned by the product's own event, never a sleep, a retry loop or a wider budget.
Find: what waitForLivePage waits for (file:line), which product event should satisfy it, and what can delay or drop that event under CI load (a worker boot ordering, a service-worker claim, the mirror's promotion, a timer the product owns); whether the 20 s budget bounds a real product wait or masks a lost event. Name the minimal cure (product-side, pinned on its own event) and the red that must fail first, with a control. Final message under 600 words.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/seat-law`>>

!! SEAT LAW (appended by tools/launch-codex.mjs to every brief; it binds this seat)
* A lane launches no Sol seat; the controller's one Sol read per train runs at the read floor of 0%.
* Stay inside the wall. Approval never escalates; a build seat has no network, loopback included; only a research seat takes `--search`. A step that needs more than the wall stops and names itself in `out.md`; the wall holds by refusal.
* Never commit and never run a git write. The lead commits each red, then each fix.
* Never build (`pnpm build`), never run vitest browser mode, never stand a vessel, socket or daemon. Typecheck (`tsc -p … --noEmit`) and run single test files that open no socket; mark any test that needs a socket "lead runs".
* A "stale build" from the dist guard stops the run; name it, and the lead builds.
* A read seat writes no file: its final message carries the hand-back. Any other seat writes `out.md` and every note in the seat directory alone. `-o` names `final.md`; stdin closes (`< /dev/null`); `TMPDIR` and `TMPPREFIX` sit inside the seat directory.
* Never run the battery; the lead holds its lock. Never read a credential file.
* Launch without `--ephemeral`: each seat keeps its rollout, so the spend tally counts it.
* The lead runs `pnpm build` in its worktree after every span merge and before each build seat; a verdict read off a stale dist counts as unread.

<<~/ahu>>

